<%# #1785: dependency-check/Dependency-Check_Action is a Docker-outside-of-Docker
    action — same defect class as bridgecrewio/checkov-action (fixed) and
    google/osv-scanner-action (fixed, #1767): on a self-hosted runner whose own
    process runs inside a container, the action's workspace bind-mount resolves
    against the DOCKER HOST path, not the runner's own checkout — and literal
    `ubuntu-latest` is no guarantee of real GitHub-hosted infra in this fleet
    (#1767). A static CLI zip (checksum-verified) has no workspace bind-mount to
    break, sidestepping the class of bug entirely. Shared partial: included from
    both _shared-security.yml.ejs (dep-cve-refresh) and 06-nightly-lite.yml.ejs
    (dep-cve-refresh) so the two java branches cannot drift apart. -%>
      - name: Install OWASP Dependency-Check (pinned CLI — no docker-container action)
        run: |
          curl -sSfL -o "$RUNNER_TEMP/dependency-check.zip" \
            https://github.com/dependency-check/DependencyCheck/releases/download/v12.1.0/dependency-check-12.1.0-release.zip
          echo "0e5ba6ae58e753d5841048c6c8e495dbc4c7a4ea921a2b14daeac65195700532  $RUNNER_TEMP/dependency-check.zip" | sha256sum -c -
          unzip -q "$RUNNER_TEMP/dependency-check.zip" -d "$RUNNER_TEMP"
          echo "$RUNNER_TEMP/dependency-check/bin" >> "$GITHUB_PATH"
      - name: OWASP Dependency-Check
        run: |
          dependency-check.sh --project '${{ github.repository }}' --scan . --format HTML --failOnCVSS 7
